SCP Idea Seeks Greenlight


17 Dec 2020 10:30






Seeking Greenlights:  Yes

Page Type:  SCP Article

Elevator Pitch: 

Doll of a non-descript female anime figure
Causes those nearby to into a near-worship state
Demands paltry tribute to stay sated
The character is unable to be described, named, nor the anime she is from
Individuals under the effect may discuss subjective traits like beauty, coolness, etc. but may not discuss any precise details of the character beyond its displayed gender and that it is an anime figurine.
When asked, individuals under the effect will reflect questions such as 'YOU don't know HER?' 'I can't believe you'd have to ask me that; a REAL fan would know.' Which draws curiosity and a potential new victim
The doll manifested due to a natural proclivity for 'otaku' obsession.
The doll represents a void of concept, it can never be fully filled as an idea, so it seeks material items to sate itself.
The student discovered the figure and gradually became a classic case of neglecting himself in favor of the idol, pushing people away while lording over them how great his new obsession was.


Central Narrative: 

The doll exists as a void of concept, and requires those nearby to give it small tokens, with no discernable pattern as to what that item needs to be. The longer that it goes without receiving a tribute, the more pressure its void will create, eventually devouring non-physical ideas and concepts.

The doll was found in a college dorm closet whose occupant began failing out due to offering term papers and other collegiate supplies. Initially thinking that the student was a hoarder, not much thought was given to the situation until the closet was forcefully cleaned and the student's roommate was found bound, malnourished, and near-death within the mass, assumed to be given as tribute when the student did not have anything else to give. Interrogation revealed that after running out of things to give the figure, the student began feeling a building pressure coming from the closet, adding to his overall stress levels as he began to notice a loss of personal identity. This lead to him offering his roommate as tribute in a panic. This information will be delivered through a series of interviews.

To remain generally inert, the item must receive a tribute every 2-3 days. However, a note from Foundation management has requested that office supplies no longer be offered due to the supply closet constantly needing to be restocked. The longer the doll goes without tribute, the stronger its pull.

Hook/Attention-Grabber: 

The doll possesses both memetic and antimemetic properties, compelling those under its effect to want to talk about her all the time but unable to physically describe any aspect that would give her characterization.





